From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_OOT_ZSTD_STREAM=1: the game's zstd stream decoder runs on the host's libzstd (svc 0xF4), with EDEN_UP_OOT_ZSTD_STREAM_VERIFY=<N> checking the first N steps against the game's own decoder (svc 0xF5); off by default

0447 (EDEN_UP_OOT_NATIVE_ZSTD) replaces the three calls of ZSTD_decompressMultiFrame, but the
loader (main+0xE8DA0) only calls that for a file that fits in one read. A larger file goes to the
game's own stream decoder: the loader fills the decode job embedded at loader+0x5A0 (vtable
main+0x4C177C0) and hands it the file one read chunk at a time, double buffered, on a job thread.
The job's run method (main+0xF5BF0) calls Step(state, chunk, size, ddict) at main+0xF5C80, a loop
of ZSTD_nextSrcSizeToDecompress / ZSTD_decompressContinue units on a buffer-less ZSTD_DCtx
(ZSTD_decompressContinue main+0xF3880, partly inlined). The game uses no ZSTD_decompressStream on
this path, so a stream-API hook would never run. The block decoder (main+0xF6490) and
HUF_decompress4X (main+0xF0860) in the page GBB's fast-mode profile names (main+0xF0000, 31% of
guest core 5 with native zstd on) are shared with ZSTD_decompressMultiFrame: with 0447 on, streams
are the main guest user of that page we know of, but nothing measured ties the 31% to them.

How it was identified: main of build E0F3CCFA... was taken out of the game's NUP (ExeFS "main",
stored raw), its ZBIC segments rewritten as plain zstd (ZBIC differs only in the magic and in a
binary-interpolative FSE count header; all three segment SHA-256s match the NSO header) and
disassembled. 0447's sites and original bytes check out against it (0xBF72E0, 0xF50164, 0xE910C,
0x14ABC, 0x58FC64). The only branch to Step is the `bl` at main+0xF5C2C (no other bl/b, no
address taken); main+0xF5C6C..0xF5C7F after its caller is zero padding nothing branches to.

With the switch, the built-in patch "Native zstd stream" turns that bl into svc 0xF4 and puts
`svc 0xF5; b 0xF5C30` at main+0xF5C70 (all-or-none, original bytes checked, build id checked).
svc 0xF4 checks the patch is in place. For a step state in phase 1 (start of a frame: nothing is
written yet and the game's Step can still run) it starts a host stream: a static host DCtx
(ZSTD_decompressBegin_usingDDict, the ddict through 0447's dictionary cache) and a 128 KiB
staging buffer, about 225 KiB, reserved in EDEN_UP_OOT_ZSTD_STREAM_BUDGET_MIB (default 16) before
anything is allocated; when the budget is full, streams idle for 10 s are evicted first. Every
step of that stream then runs Step's own unit loop on the host and decodes straight into the
guest destination through its host pointer: the destination has to be one contiguous host block
(checked page by page at the start and for each block), and there is no window buffer. Same
units and the same staging (a raw block split over two chunks waits, as in the game), so after
each step the bytes written, +0x08, +0x10/+0x14, +0x2C, the phase (2/3/4) and the return value
(-1, -2 for dstSize_tooSmall, -3 for input after the frame end) are the game's. Before and after
each block the bytes it may write go through Memory::FlushDataCache: HandleRasterizerWrite for
pages the GPU caches track, as WriteBlock calls it before it copies (the ahead guard copies such
a page there). One difference stays: host libzstd 1.5 may put a block's literals up to one block
ahead of +0x08, in bytes that are not decoded yet either way. The game's DCtx is never
initialised; +0x30 (0 from the loader) stays 0 as the host's mark, so a host stream that was lost
or evicted, or a step state changed behind the host, fails the step (phase 3, -1) instead of
running the game's decoder on an empty DCtx. Anything the host does not reproduce (skippable,
empty or unknown-size frame, a destination smaller than the content or not one host block, an
unusual dictionary, budget full, a failed allocation) runs the game's Step for the whole stream.
Live switch (0478): EDEN_UP_OOT_ZSTD_STREAM is a new armed entry, read only when a stream starts,
so a stream never changes owner; in an off phase new streams go to the game.

EDEN_UP_OOT_ZSTD_STREAM_VERIFY=<N>: a check run. The host owns no stream; the game's Step decodes
everything. For the first N steps (each stream from its first step on) Step returns into the
cave, whose svc 0xF5 decodes the same chunk on the host into a window of its own
(ZSTD_decodingBufferSize_min, charged to the budget) and compares each unit's bytes with what the
game wrote, then the return value, the phase and +0x08/+0x10/+0x14/+0x2C (the run method keeps
the job in x19). Only streams that started take steps. Equal steps log 16 lines, mismatches up
to 16 lines with the first differing byte, plus a verify counters line every second (streams
whose window does not fit the budget are counted as not checked: raise the budget for the check
run if there are many). After N steps the game goes on alone.
Counters: "Native zstd stream: ..." once a second while streams run.

Unset: no built-in patch, svc 0xF4/0xF5 return false before anything else, as before, and the
live switch is never read. Not compiled: needs a build, then one VERIFY run (e.g. VERIFY=2000 on
the door benchmark) with zero mismatches before any fps run.
---
